From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cybermiku <cybermiku@local>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:10:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] state: always restore cwd after set_stdio

set_stdio() chains its conditions with short-circuit OR, so when any
freopen() fails (e.g. /dev/console open returns ENXIO on a system
without a working console) the trailing chdir("/") is never executed
and procd's working directory stays at /dev forever.

During sysupgrade, procd chroots into the RAM prefix and execs
upgraded, which performs chroot("."). Since cwd lies outside the
current root, this resets the root directory to the stale cwd (/dev),
so execvp("/lib/upgrade/stage2") resolves to /dev/lib/upgrade/stage2,
fails with ENOENT, the upgrade aborts and the device reboots without
writing the image.

Always restore the cwd to / even when redirecting stdio fails.
---
 state.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/state.c b/state.c
--- a/state.c
+++ b/state.c
@@ -48,8 +48,10 @@
 	if (chdir("/dev") ||
 	    !freopen(tty, "r", stdin) ||
 	    !freopen(tty, "w", stdout) ||
-	    !freopen(tty, "w", stderr) ||
-	    chdir("/"))
+	    !freopen(tty, "w", stderr)) {
+		ERROR("failed to set stdio: %m\n");
+		chdir("/");
+	} else if (chdir("/"))
 		ERROR("failed to set stdio: %m\n");
 	else
 		fcntl(STDERR_FILENO, F_SETFL, fcntl(STDERR_FILENO, F_GETFL) | O_NONBLOCK);
